THREE EXCEPTIONS

1. Sanskrit source passages. The `source_passage_verbatim` fields in
   `taxonomy/hetvabhasa_v2.2.json` hold nine short sentences from Annambhatta's
   Tarkasamgraha, a seventeenth-century work in the public domain. They are
   reproduced as brief quotations, for identification and scholarly reference.
   This repository claims no copyright in them.

   The copy consulted was the electronic text published by the Goettingen
   Register of Electronic Texts in Indian Languages (GRETIL), data entry by
   Takuya Ono, TEI version of 2020-07-31, for which thanks:

       https://zenodo.org/records/6466333

   GRETIL distributes that complete e-text under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, and anyone
   wanting the whole text should obtain it from GRETIL under those terms. That
   licence is not asserted here over the nine quoted sentences, which are the
   words of a public-domain work rather than of the e-text. The English glosses
   beside them, the category structure and all surrounding material are ours and
   fall under CC BY 4.0.

2. LOGIC and MAFALDA. Neither dataset states a licence, so neither is
   redistributed here. Files under `vyapti/data/crossmap/` and
   `vyapti/data/external/` carry row references and hashes only.
   `vyapti/scripts/fetch_external.py` retrieves the texts from the original
   repositories at pinned commits, under whatever terms those repositories set.
